## Workspace

Clay workspace: {{WORKSPACE_URL}} — "{{WORKSPACE_NAME}}"

## Folder structure (always true, don't re-derive this)

- `{{EVENTS_FOLDER}}`: one workbook per competitor event, named **exactly**
  after its scraper folder. No reformatting, no added suffixes.
- `{{BLOCKLIST_TABLE}}`: lives **one level up** from `{{EVENTS_FOLDER}}`,
  not inside it. Shared cross-event registry (Company Name, Company Domain)
  — every company that passes through this pipeline's main table gets
  logged here.

## The one hard rule: what's allowed to actually run

Only three things call a paid provider per row — **configure these but
never trigger a full run**: any Claygent/AI column, the `Enrich Company`
action, and any Find People run.

Everything else — creating tables and workbooks, importing CSVs, formula
columns, Send Table Data actions — should be **created and actually
executed**. None of it costs credits, so there's no reason to leave it
configured-but-dormant.

## Full build procedure

Rendered per-event build spec: run
`python template/render_build_prompt.py --entity <entity> --icp <icp>`
from this repo, or read `docs/PIPELINE_ARCHITECTURE.md` for the generic
version. Any ICP-specific open issues (e.g. an unresolved tiering
discrepancy) are in `config/icps/<icp>/icp.yaml: known_issues` and
`docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md` — don't silently resolve those.

## Source files expected in this folder

- The ICP playbook workbook (source of truth for taxonomies,
  segment/category names, and tier logic) — kept local, not in git; see
  `docs/SENSITIVE_DATA.md`.
- Per-event scraper folders, each containing its own normalized CSV for
  this entity type.
